- op: discuss  # 6941
  at: '2026-11-17T19:36:03Z'  # 6941
  by: agent  # 6941
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 6941
  clock: 4  # 6941
  nonce: '6941'  # 6941
  message: "Fixed in PR #2235 (dev a60b1a86d): selection_index.update_from_run counts a test as having produced rows only when a row is in its own call phase (pytest-cov's |run context, or a context with no phase); rows from |setup and |teardown stay edges and no longer clear the unmeasured flag or make the test a producer of its run record. BEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE, the item's own repro re-run on the real index after a full re-fold (2026-11-17 19:35 UTC; output in ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/fast_smart_test_build_11172026/fixture_row_hole.txt): (1) the full run's fold printed 'full run: coverage cannot speak for 8704 test(s) (their own call ran no measured code); 227 before this run' (41,094 passed); (2) the same command as filed, same one-statement edit to graph_rows.walk, same 10-file run set: 'narrow: 10 -> 10 file(s), dropped 0', exit 0, where it had dropped 7; test_smart_test_recorders.py is among the kept; (3) narrowing still narrows: 1,225 test files are droppable for a change to graph_rows.py (1,461 while the defect held). Tests: test_selection_index_own_phase.py (7 tests, the hole reproduced in miniature and at the command), 10 mutations each red. NOT ESTABLISHED: which of the 12 test files removed from the 4 narrowed manifests committed between the fixture (b962b6cc6) and the fix (26f51346b 2 files, d0e00a83c 1, eec3215e6 8, 5a38b95bb 1) were removed because of the defect. Bound: two full local runs on dev since (41,087 and 41,094 tests) passed, so no removed test is failing on dev. NOT CLOSED BY THIS: a test whose own call runs some measured code in process AND does other work in a subprocess is still called measured; that shape predates the fixture and has no item of its own that I know of. NO STRUCTURAL GUARD beyond the printed count: a sharp fall in that number has to be noticed by a reader."  # 6941
